{%- comment -%}
  The competition card.

  Four things, in this order: the image, the prize, the entry price, the action.
  Everything else belongs on the competition page.

  The card carries a live availability count, taken from Shopify inventory
  rather than the hand-maintained entries_sold metafield. It is a number and
  never a bar: a count is information, a filling meter is pressure.

  Still deliberately absent:
    - No progress bar. See above, and docs/PERSUASION.md.
    - One badge maximum, never two. Three urgency signals on one card is how a
      competition site starts to look like a slot machine.
    - No gold anywhere. Brass means winners and nothing else.

  The "Win a" prefix is trimmed only when settings.card_trim_win_prefix is on.
  It ships off: "Win a TaylorMade Qi10 Driver" is the thing the visitor wants,
  and stating it plainly is the whole commercial proposition of the card.

  Parameters:
    product          (required)
    variant          'default' or 'compact'
    image_ratio      override the theme setting
    loading          'lazy' (default) or 'eager'
    sizes            sizes attribute for the image
    show_progress    override the theme setting
    show_availability override the theme setting
    show_prize_value override the theme setting
    show_closing     override the theme setting
    show_badges      override the theme setting
    heading_tag      'h3' (default)
    index            position in the list, used for analytics
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign ratio = image_ratio | default: settings.card_image_ratio | default: 'portrait'
  assign heading = heading_tag | default: 'h3'
  assign img_loading = loading | default: 'lazy'
  assign img_sizes = sizes | default: '(min-width: 990px) 340px, (min-width: 600px) 45vw, 45vw'

  assign with_progress = show_progress
  if with_progress == nil
    assign with_progress = settings.card_show_progress
  endif
  assign with_prize_value = show_prize_value
  if with_prize_value == nil
    assign with_prize_value = settings.card_show_prize_value
  endif
  assign with_closing = show_closing
  if with_closing == nil
    assign with_closing = settings.card_show_closing
  endif
  assign with_badges = show_badges
  if with_badges == nil
    assign with_badges = settings.card_show_badges
  endif
  comment
    Availability has no theme setting behind it, unlike the other card fields.
    The snippet renders nothing unless a real cap exists and Shopify is
    tracking inventory, so a switch could only ever hide a figure that is
    true. Pass show_availability: false to suppress it in a specific context.
  endcomment
  assign with_availability = show_availability
  if with_availability == nil
    assign with_availability = true
  endif

  assign prize_value = product.metafields.custom.prize_value
  assign closing_at = product.metafields.custom.closing_at.value

  assign is_closed = false
  if closing_at != blank
    assign now_stamp = 'now' | date: '%s' | times: 1
    assign close_stamp = closing_at | date: '%s' | times: 1
    if close_stamp <= now_stamp
      assign is_closed = true
    endif
  endif

  assign can_enter = product.available
  if is_closed
    assign can_enter = false
  endif

  assign cta_label = settings.entry_cta_label | default: 'Enter'
  unless can_enter
    assign cta_label = 'products.competition.view_competition' | t
  endunless

  comment
    Trim a leading "Win a" / "Win an" / "Win the". The card sits under a heading
    that already establishes what these are, and those two words were occupying
    the most visible line of the most repeated component on the site.

    Only the first character is raised. The `capitalize` filter lowercases
    everything after it, which turns "TaylorMade Qi10" into "Taylormade qi10" —
    unacceptable on a site whose entire proposition is the brand of the prize.
  endcomment
  assign card_title = product.title
  if settings.card_trim_win_prefix
    assign lower_title = card_title | downcase
    if lower_title contains 'win a '
      assign card_title = card_title | remove_first: 'Win a ' | remove_first: 'win a ' | remove_first: 'WIN A '
    elsif lower_title contains 'win an '
      assign card_title = card_title | remove_first: 'Win an ' | remove_first: 'win an ' | remove_first: 'WIN AN '
    elsif lower_title contains 'win the '
      assign card_title = card_title | remove_first: 'Win the ' | remove_first: 'win the ' | remove_first: 'WIN THE '
    endif

    assign title_length = card_title | size
    if title_length > 1
      assign first_letter = card_title | slice: 0 | upcase
      assign remainder = card_title | slice: 1, title_length
      assign card_title = first_letter | append: remainder
    endif
  endif

  comment
    Whole pounds, and no currency code. `metafield_text` renders a money
    metafield as "£600.00 GBP", so stripping only ".00" left "£600 GBP value"
    on every card. `prize_value.value` is the amount in the shop's minor unit,
    and the money filter formats it with the shop's own symbol. Not
    `.value.amount`, which reads as empty and removes the line altogether.
  endcomment
  assign prize_value_text = ''
  if prize_value != blank
    assign prize_value_text = prize_value.value | money | remove: '.00'
  endif

  assign card_alt = product.featured_media.alt | default: product.title
-%}

<article
  class="competition-card{% if variant == 'compact' %} competition-card--compact{% endif %}{% unless can_enter %} competition-card--unavailable{% endunless %}"
  data-competition-card
  data-product-id="{{ product.id }}"
>
  <div class="competition-card__media media media--{{ ratio }}">
    {%- if product.featured_media -%}
      {%- render 'responsive-image',
        image: product.featured_media,
        alt: card_alt,
        sizes: img_sizes,
        loading: img_loading,
        widths: '340,440,560,720,900,1080'
      -%}
    {%- else -%}
      {%- render 'placeholder', name: 'product-1' -%}
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if with_badges -%}
      {%- render 'competition-badges', product: product, max: 1 -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>

  <div class="competition-card__body">
    <{{ heading }} class="competition-card__title">
      <a
        class="competition-card__link"
        href="{{ product.url }}"
        data-track="competition_card_click"
        data-track-payload='{"product_id":{{ product.id }},"position":{{ index | default: 0 }}}'
      >
        {{- card_title | escape -}}
      </a>
    </{{ heading }}>

    {%- if with_prize_value and prize_value_text != blank -%}
      <p class="competition-card__value num">{{ prize_value_text }} value</p>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if with_closing -%}
      {%- capture closing_markup -%}{%- render 'competition-closing', product: product, icon: false -%}{%- endcapture -%}
      {%- if closing_markup != blank -%}
        <p class="competition-card__closing num">{{ closing_markup }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- comment -%}
      How many entries are left, from live inventory rather than the
      hand-maintained entries_sold metafield. A count, never a filling bar:
      the number is the information, the meter is the pressure. See
      docs/PERSUASION.md and snippets/competition-availability.liquid.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if with_availability -%}
      {%- render 'competition-availability', product: product, mode: 'left' -%}
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if with_progress -%}
      {%- render 'competition-progress', product: product, size: 'small' -%}
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- comment -%}
      The spacer sits above the footer so that every card in a row lands its
      price and action on the same baseline, whatever optional lines it carries.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="competition-card__spacer"></div>

    <div class="competition-card__footer">
      <p class="competition-card__price">
        <span class="competition-card__price-amount num">
          {%- if product.price_varies -%}
            {%- assign min_price = product.price_min | money -%}
            {{- 'products.product.from_price' | t: price: min_price -}}
          {%- else -%}
            {{- product.price | money -}}
          {%- endif -%}
        </span>
        <span class="competition-card__price-label">
          {{- 'products.competition.per_entry' | t -}}
        </span>
      </p>

      <span class="competition-card__cta" aria-hidden="true">
        {{- cta_label }}
        {%- render 'icon', icon: 'arrow-right', size: 14 -%}
      </span>
    </div>
  </div>
</article>
